00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.720
Okay, so lots of big stuff to get through. Lots of Easter Eggs. 

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.340
So let's just start with 'Top 5 Moments':

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.500
Careful fore spoilers if you haven't seen the episode yet.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.340
No. 5: Team Flash starts to understand the Firestorm Matrix.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:08.080
The beginning of the episode picks up IMMEDIATELY after last week's episode.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.240
So, whenever you're watching this in the future, just watch 'em back to back

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.020
and It'll be like a 2-hour episode.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.400
The 1ˢᵗ half was all about introducing Firestorm.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.820
2ᴺᴰ half all about understanding what it's gonna be like going forward.

00:01:18.941 --> 00:01:22.461
So by the end of the episode they figure it out a little bit better, and they can coexist 

00:01:22.461 --> 00:01:25.661
inside the Firestorm Matrix as distinct personalities.

00:01:25.661 --> 00:01:28.161
That 'floaty-head-voice' that you heard from Martin Stein? 

00:01:28.161 --> 00:01:29.141
...that's how it is in the comics.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.120
A lot of the bickering they did is also from the Firestorm comics too.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.781
(that's part of the dynamic between Ronnie Raymond and Martin Stein)

00:01:35.781 --> 00:01:36.640
On to No. 4: 

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.160
Iris West is going to start investigating Star Labs.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:46.580
They just teased it in the episode, but what I feel like is gonna happen is Iris WILL learn Barry is the Flash by the end of the season.

00:01:46.589 --> 00:01:51.381
She'll be investigating Star Labs because of all these mysterious metahumans; all this crazy stuff going on.

00:01:51.381 --> 00:01:54.248
And as a consequence of that, she'll learn that Barry's "The Flash".

00:01:54.248 --> 00:01:59.567
Eventually, what I'd like to see, is her become the focal-point of the battle between the Flash and the Reverse Flash.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.499
And, possibly the creation of a 2ᴺᴰ Reverse Flash

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.340
I know in the promo for E15 we saw Harrison Wells use the Speed Force to split himself in two --

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.880
to make it appear like there were two of him

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.200
-- but I'm expecting ANOTHER Reverse Flash.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.620
Like an 'Eddie Thawne' Reverse Flash to be created by the end of the season.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:15.640
On to No. 3:

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:19.320
Harrison Wells helps General Eiling capture Martin Stein. 

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.550
I saw a lot of people were confused about this on Twitter.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:27.180
You know, "Why would Harrison Wells help* General Eiling, if he wants to help* Team Flash, and learn more about Firestorm?"

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.000
Well, really, it's that second thing.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.380
I think he just wanted to learn more about the nature of Firestorm's powers.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.040
I think he was telling the truth when he said,

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.020
"I don't understand how Firestorm works"

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:41.260
Knowing that he, AS the Reverse Flash, is weak against Firestorm's powers (like we learned in E09)

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.820
he prob'ly wants to learn as much as he can about him.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.820
Supposedly Firestorm is gonna be back for the finale.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.600
It hasn't been confirmed by the CW. 

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.020
I don't know what he's gonna be doing.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:54.855
I'm HOPING that the Reverse Flash uses Firestorm's powers to enact some plot.

00:02:54.855 --> 00:02:57.320
...but he might just come back to help fight the Reverse Flash.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:00.880
They wouldn't bring the character back just to have a pizza party with Team Flash;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.729
so whatever's happening, Firestorm is important to the finale.

00:03:04.729 --> 00:03:05.840
Moving on to No. 2:

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.164
Barry is going to use his knowledge of the past to try'nd save his mother.

00:03:10.164 --> 00:03:12.404
So they're slowly pushing into time travel.

00:03:12.404 --> 00:03:15.780
I like the way they compared 'Back to the Future' rules, and 'Terminator' rules.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:19.220
Really what you need to watch out for, is, "Predestination Paradox":

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.480
Whereby, if he changes the past (if he saves his mother) it might prevent him from

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:28.220
ever becoming the Flash, and therefore being able to go back in time and save his mother.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.359
If you've seen the animated movie, "Flashpoint", this is what it's all about.

00:03:31.359 --> 00:03:32.950
Barry goes back. Saves his mother.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:36.490
And it COMPLETELY messes up the timeline; everything goes bananas.~ 

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.190
(To make another Gorilla Grodd joke)

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:41.920
Just feel free to make any 'Grodd/Bananas' jokes you want throughout this video.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:45.480
There was an earlier episode this season, where Joe tells Barry,

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.600
"You need to learn to live with the things that you can't change"

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.520
So, that's gonna be part of his arc this season:

00:03:50.552 --> 00:03:52.892
Learning that he can't* save his mother.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.640
...no matter how powerful he gets.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:57.420
The same thing is true for the Reverse Flash in the comics:

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.140
The 'Professor Zoom' Reverse Flash.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.380
He hates Barry Allen. 

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.514
Wants to kill him. 

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.800
But if he kills Barry Allen, then he'll never become the Reverse Flash in the future.

00:04:05.963 --> 00:04:09.620
So both the Flash, and the Reverse Flash, are stuck in this causality loop.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.460
And, my No. 1 Moment (obviously):

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.240
Not God...GRODD.

00:04:13.545 --> 00:04:15.980
THE best end-credits scene ALL season.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:20.420
Not only does Harrison Wells unmask himself to someone as the Reverse Flash

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:24.920
we also get to hear Grodd speak AND use his powers of mind control.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.600
The TV show is playing a little bit with the origin stories.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.440
Harrison Wells confirms that he is a metahuman.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.093
But, technically, the Flash isn't a metahuman.

00:04:33.093 --> 00:04:38.758
"Metahumans" (as the show defines them) were people that got powers because of the Dark-Matter Explosion.

00:04:38.758 --> 00:04:43.878
The Flash and the Reverse Flash both got their powers from the Speed Force (and the Negative Speed Force).

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.980
Which is not part of the Dark-Matter in the comics.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:48.540
But I think the show is just combining those things.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:49.040
So.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.260
Technically you could* call the Flash a metahuman.

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:54.820
This doesn't really change anything that we didn't already know about Harrison Wells.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:55.760
Other than when he said,

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.080
"I take care of my own"

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:00.640
It's interesting to think that he is "protecting" the other metahumans.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:05.820
Whenever we first got that Gorilla Grodd-flashback, it seemed like he cared for him (like he was trying to help him).

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:09.134
It humanizes him a little bit, but there's a very nefarious undertone.

00:05:09.134 --> 00:05:15.120
It's like, "Yes I'm going to protect this Gorilla, but only so I can use him to do something really aweful".

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.920
And in the promo for E15, he basically calls Barry Allen, a 'surrogate son'.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.691
In the comics, Professor Zoom---Eobard Thawne---isn't like that at all.

00:05:23.691 --> 00:05:24.591
He's completely nuts.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:25.600
He hates everyone.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:30.500
So this is the show just softening that character and using some aspects from Hunter Zolomon's character

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:34.560
in the comics. So what you're getting is, an amalgam, of Reverse Flashes.

00:05:34.568 --> 00:05:38.580
And eventually, when we get a 3ᴿᴰ Reverse Flash (when we get like our 'Eddie Thawne' Reverse Flash)

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.950
I think the same thing'll happen.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.468
He'll ALSO be an amalgam of a couple of Reverse Flashes.

00:05:42.468 --> 00:05:45.548
One of the biggest questions you guys had after last week's episode was,

00:05:45.548 --> 00:05:49.940
"When is Team Flash gonna learn what Harrison Wells is doing (that he's the Reverse Flash)?"

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.780
And the promo for E15 seems like it totally answers that.

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:56.180
Meaning that there's like 8 episodes left in the season.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:00.000
DOES that not get you SO FREAKING EXCITED for where they're going to take the show?

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:00.760
Lemme know though:

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.140
What was your favorite moment from the episode?

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.500
And here's my big question:

00:06:03.507 --> 00:06:09.050
What do you think that Harrison Wells is going to do, once that he reveals himself to Barry, as the Reverse Flash?

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:13.390
It's definitely gonna break their relationship once Barry learns that he's the "Man in Yellow".

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:16.300
Remember what Harrison Wells said though (when he was talking about Firestorm):

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.660
"Accept each other"

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.280
"Accept the balance between you"

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.915
He was talking about Ronnie Raymond and Martin Stein accepting each other.

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:27.560
But, really, the double-meaning is the Flash needs to learn to accept the Reverse Flash.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.340
Tom Cavanagh. Amazing actor.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:35.880
He was really open during the TCA's earlier this year about how he built in double-meanings to each of his lines.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.580
I know sometimes, when he says one thing it sounds like he might be dropping Easter eggs for something else.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.460
...it's totally true.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.040
He's doing that all the time.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:46.697
So just remember that whenever you hear him saying something that sounds really suspicious.

00:06:46.697 --> 00:06:50.082
Here are some of the really cool Easter Eggs that I found that I haven't already mentioned yet:

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:55.840
Both Martin Stein and Ronnie Raymond, when they're separated, heat up to about a 106°F (41°C) resting temperature.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:59.940
Issue #106 of The Flash, was the debut of Gorilla Grodd.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.700
Obviously we saw Gorilla Grodd, full on, at the end of the episode.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:05.400
 When Barry goes back into his old house and said,

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.370
"That mirror belonged to my Grandmother"

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.975
(Iris West-Allen)

00:07:09.015 --> 00:07:13.535
Obviously she gets married to Barry Allen in the comics; they have children; their children have children.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:17.140
SO Iris West-Allen becomes the grandmother of the 'Bart Allen' Flash.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:21.520
In the episode, they're using the mirror to look into the past, but it's also an Easter Egg 

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:24.580
for what's going to happen in the future, for the future of the Flash Lineage.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:32.760
When Martin Stein talks about time traveling using a "highway" -- really that's the Speed Force (the Speed Force IS the highway).

00:07:32.769 --> 00:07:36.663
Moving so fast that you punch a hole in the space-time continuum.

00:07:36.663 --> 00:07:39.639
We're supposedly gonna get a teaser for that in E15.

00:07:39.639 --> 00:07:41.459
But I have no idea what it's going to look like.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:43.620
Caitlin mentions Jason Rush Again.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:46.880
Jason Rush also become part of the Firestorm Matrix in the comics.

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:51.320
It seems like they're going to stick with Martin Stein and Ronnie Raymond---with that pairing---through S02.

00:07:51.640 --> 00:07:55.980
They say that Ronnie is Caitlin's cousin from Coast City (that's obviously where Green Lantern's from).

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.740
I know we all want to see him on the show at some point.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.080
Martin Stein talks to Harrison Wells and says, 

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.220
"I should have spent my life trying to be the best husband I could for my wife."

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:07.540
I feel like that was a loaded moment because it makes you think of Harrison Wells' dead wife.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:12.540
Which is prob'ly the reason he's trying to gain the powers of the Flash; so that he can go back in time and save his wife.

00:08:12.794 --> 00:08:15.346
It's romantic, in a really pathological way.

00:08:15.346 --> 00:08:16.586
This is a really funny one:

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:21.980
Ronnie Raymond etches the message into his arm so that it appears on Martin Stein's arm.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:27.440
But instead of scratching the answer on HIS arm, Martin Stein just taps Morse Code.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.220
The reason it's funny is because Ronnie didn't* need to cut himself.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:31.460
He could've used Morse Code too.

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:36.720
When Ronnie says Martin Stein has a friend in Pittsburgh that can help 'em, it's actually and Easter Egg for the comics.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:39.460
Ronnie Raymond, in the comics, is from Pittsburgh.

00:08:39.467 --> 00:08:41.567
At the end of the episode General Eiling says, 

00:08:41.567 --> 00:08:42.747
"That voice in my head"

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:45.000
That's just a reference to Gorilla Grodd's powers.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.580
He has powers of mind control.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:50.040
Cisco says, "I bet you that's where they're keeping the aliens too"

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:54.220
That could've been an Easter Egg for Martian Manhunter, or Superman from Flashpoint.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:57.754
If you guys did see any other Easter Eggs in the episode just write 'em below in the comments.

00:08:57.754 --> 00:09:01.080
The only real Thumbs Down I had in the episode was the Iris West storyline.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:05.860
I feel like it's really far behind. It's moving WAY slower than all the other storylines.

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:07.700
It's lagging behind...big time.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:13.800
I feel like something really big is gonna have to happen in the next 3 or 4 episodes to bring Iris West to the forefront of the story.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:16.769
That's probably gonna be the investigation into Star Labs.

00:09:16.769 --> 00:09:19.108
So hopefully that'll happen sooner*, rather than later.

00:09:19.108 --> 00:09:21.272
Candace Patton is a great actress.

00:09:21.272 --> 00:09:24.980
But I feel like Iris West's character hasn't caught up with the rest of the show yet.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.800
Since there's no new episode of The Flash next week, I'm just gonna do a bonus video.

00:09:28.807 --> 00:09:30.100
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.043
Feel free to leave me any requests you guys want.

00:09:32.043 --> 00:09:36.280
And, remember, new episode of Arrow tomorrow -- and another new episode of Arrow next week.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:39.300
While you guys wait for that stuff, you can click here* to get ready for Arrow.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:42.460
And, you can click here* to watch last week's episode of The Flash.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:43.360
Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.920
So let's all high five. I'll see you guys tomorrow.

